{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function notifyhdb to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "notifyhdb:{[h;d]\n\t/-if you can connect to the hdb - call the reload function \n\t@[h;hdbmessage[d];{.lg.e[`notifyhdb;\"failed to send reload message to hdb on handle: \",x]}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function tablecount to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "tablecount:{[par]\n  .lg.o[`tablecount;\"Getting table count dictionary\"];\n  /- create dictionary of partition tables with their counts\n  .Q.pt!{[par;x]count ?[x;enlist(=;.Q.pf;par);0b;()]}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement duplicateconfig in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "duplicateconfig:{[t] update proc:raze[t `proc] from ((select from t)where count each t[`proc])}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "writedown:{\n  if[0=count .dqe.tosavedown`.dqe.results;:()];\n  .dqe.savedata[.dqe.dqcdbdir;.dqe.getpartition[];.dqe.tosavedown`.dqe.results;`.dqe;`results];\n  /- get handles for DBs that need to reload\n  hdbs:distinct raze exec w from .servers.SERVERS where proctype=`dqcdb;\n  /- send message for DBs to reload\n  .dqe.notifyhdb[.os.pth .dqe.dqcdbdir]'[hdbs];\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function writedownconfig to execute a query and return results", "input": "", "output": "writedownconfig:{\n  if[0=count .dqe.tosavedown`.dqe.configtable;:()];\n  .dqe.savedata[.dqe.dqcdbdir;.dqe.getpartition[];.dqe.tosavedown`.dqe.configtable;`.dqe;`configtable];\n  /- get handles for DBsthat need to reload\n  hdbs:distinct raze exec w from .servers.SERVERS where proctype=`dqcdb;\n  /- send message for DB\n  .dqe.notifyhdb[.os.pth .dqe.dqcdbdir]'[hdbs];\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function dupchk to query and filter table data", "input": "", "output": "dupchk:{[runtype;idnum;params;proc]\n  if[params`comp;proc:params`compresproc];\n  if[`=proc;:()];\n  if[count select from .dqe.results where id=idnum,procschk=proc,chkstatus=`started;\n    .dqe.updresultstab[runtype;idnum;0Np;0b;\"error:fail to complete before next run\";`failed;params;proc]];\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named chkcompare that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "chkcompare:{[runtype;idnum;params]\n  /- checks if all async check results have returned - if not, exit the function\n  if[params[`compcount]<>(d:.dqe.compcounter idnum)`counter;:()];\n  .lg.o[`chkcompare;\"comparison started with id \",string idnum];\n  /- obtain all the check returns\n  a:d[`results] where not d[`procs]=params`compproc;\n  procsforcomp:d[`procs] except params`compproc;\n  /- obtain the check to compare the others to\n  b:d[`results] where d[`procs]=params`compproc;\n\n  /- if error in compare proc then fail check\n  if[@[{all 0W=x}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement loadsym in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "loadsym:{[]\n    .lg.o[`load;\"loading the sym file\"];\n    @[load;symfilepath; {.lg.e[`load;\"failed to load sym file: \",string[symfilepath],\" error: \",x]}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function loadidb to load data from files or databases", "input": "", "output": "loadidb:{[]\n    .lg.o[`load;\"loading the db\"];\n    @[system; \"l \", 1_string idbdir; {.lg.e[`load;\"failed to load IDB: \",string[idbdir],\" error: \",x]}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function loaddb that load data from files or databases", "input": "", "output": "loaddb:{[]\n    starttime:.proc.ct[];\n    loadsym[];\n    loadidb[];\n    .lg.o[`load;\"IDB load has been finished for partition: \",string[currentpartition],\". Time taken(ms): \",string .proc.ct[]-starttime];\n }"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for rollover to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "rollover:{[pt]\n    currentpartition::pt;\n    idbdir::.Q.dd[savedir; $[writedownmode~`default;`;currentpartition]];\n    .lg.o[`rollover;\"IDB folder has been set to: \",string[idbdir]];\n    loaddb[];\n }"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named intradayreload that load data from files or databases", "input": "", "output": "intradayreload:{[]\n    starttime:.proc.ct[];\n    if[symfilehaschanged[];loadsym[]];\n    if[partitioncounthaschanged[];loadidb[]];\n    clearrowcountcache[];\n    .lg.o[`intradayreload;\"IDB reload has been finished for partition: \",string[currentpartition],\". Time taken(ms): \",string .proc.ct[]-starttime];\n }"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named subdetails that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "subdetails:{[tabs;instruments]\n `schemalist`logfilelist`rowcounts`date`logdir!(.ps.subscribe\\:[tabs;instruments];.stplg.replaylog[tabs];tabs#.stplg `rowcount;(.eodtime `d);.stplg.kdbtplog)\n }"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement generateschemas in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "generateschemas:{\n  .stpps.init[tables[] except `currlog`heartbeat`logmsg`svrstoload];\n  .stpps.attrstrip[.stpps.t];\n\n  // Table UPD functions attach the current timestamp by default, if STP is chained these do nothing\n  $[.sctp.chainedtp;\n    .stplg.updtab:(.stpps.t!(count .stpps.t)#{[x;y] x}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named loadschemas that load data from files or databases", "input": "", "output": "loadschemas:{\n  if[not `schemafile in key .proc.params;.lg.e[`loadschema;\"Schema file required!\"];exit 1];\n  @[.proc.loadf;raze .proc.params[`schemafile];{.lg.e[`loadschema;\"Failed to load schema file!\"];exit 1}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function setup to initialize or configure the system", "input": "", "output": "setup:{[batch]\n  // Handle bad batch mode, see whether STP is chained or default\n  if[not all batch in/: key'[.stplg`upd`zts];'\"mode \",(string batch),\" must be defined in both .stplg.upd and .stplg.zts\"];\n  chainmode:$[.sctp.chainedtp;`chained;`def];\n\n  // Set inner UPD and ZTS behaviour from batch mode, then set outer functions based on whether STP is chained\n  .stplg.updmsg:.stplg.upd[batch];\n  .stplg.ts:.stplg.zts[batch];\n  .u.upd:.stpps.upd[chainmode];\n  .dotz.set[`.z.ts;\n    {[f;x] @[;x;()]each f}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement upd in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "upd:{[t;x] .[.stp.upd;(t;x);{.stplg.badmsg[x;y;z]}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named starttests that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "starttests:{[]\n  // Check if ready to start tests - retry connection if not ready\n  if[(exec any null w from .servers.SERVERS where proctype=`rdb)|(not`upd in key`.u)|(not`upd in key`.stp)|not`nextendUTC in key`.stplg;.servers.retry[]];\n  // Check again after retrying connection - return if still not ready\n  if[(exec any null w from .servers.SERVERS where proctype=`rdb)|(not`upd in key`.u)|(not`upd in key`.stp)|not`nextendUTC in key`.stplg;:()];\n\n  // Once connection ready - clear timer and start tests\n  remove[1];\n  system\"l \",getenv[`perfpath],\"/run_perf_test.q\";\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named backfill that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "backfill:{[dqetab;funct;vars;proc;dateof;dir]\n  / - empty the table from memory first\n  .dqe.cleartables[`.dqe;dqetab];\n  / - funct represents the dqe query that you would like to perform on the older data from an old date(dateof)\n  .dqe.runquery[funct;(vars;dateof);`table;proc];\n  .dqe.savedata[dir;dateof;.dqe.tosavedown[.Q.dd[`.dqe;dqetab]];`.dqe;dqetab];\n  .dqe.cleartables[`.dqe;dqetab];\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement meterusage in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "meterusage:{[startdate; enddate]\n \n /- calculate the usage at the start and the end\n start:select first usage by meterid from meter where date=startdate;\n end:select last usage by meterid from meter where date=enddate;\n \n /- subtract the two\n end-start}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function monthlyusage that query and filter table data", "input": "", "output": "monthlyusage:{[month] \n `month`meterid xkey \n  select month:month,meterid,usage \n  from meterusage[`date$month; -1+`date$month+1]}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named monthlyusagebycusttype that group data by key columns", "input": "", "output": "monthlyusagebycusttype:{[months] \n select sum usage by month,custtype \n from \n  (raze monthlyusage peach months,:()) \n  lj \n  `meterid xkey select meterid,custtype from static}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for meterusagepivot to calculate aggregate statistics", "input": "", "output": "meterusagepivot:{[startdate;enddate;aspercent]\n t:meterusage[startdate;enddate];\n \n /- join on the static data\n t:t lj static;\n \n /- Calculate the total usage for each grouping\n t:select sum usage by custtype,region from t;\n \n /- Convert to % values\n if[aspercent;t:update usage:100*usage%sum usage from t];\n \n /- pivot the data to have the regions as row ids\n /- and the customer types as the column headers\n C:asc exec distinct custtype from t;\n t1:exec C#custtype!usage by region:region from t;\n \n /- fill the pivot table with 0s\n 0^t1}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for meterusagejump to filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "meterusagejump:{[startdate;enddate;daycount;rangecheck]\n /- pull out the daily starting values\n t:select first usage by date,meterid from meter where date within (startdate;enddate);\n\n /- calculate the daily usage\n t:update usage:next deltas usage by meterid from t;\n\n /- add the moving average\n t:update mavgusage:daycount mavg usage by meterid from t;\n\n /- pull out the rows which are outside the range check\n select from t where rangecheck < abs 100*1 - usage % mavgusage}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that load data from files or databases", "input": "", "output": "loadcsv:{[inputcsv]\n    compressioncsv::@[{.lg.o[`compression;\"Opening \", x];(\"SISIII\"; enlist \",\") 0:\"S\"$x}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for traverse to filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "traverse:{$[(0=count k)or x~k:key x; x; .z.s each ` sv' x,/:k where not any k like/:(\".d\";\"*.q\";\"*.k\";\"*#\")]}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named age that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "age:{$[all x within 1000 3000; x - `year$.z.D;(count x)#0Ni]}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function compressfromtable to update table records", "input": "", "output": "compressfromtable:{[table]\n    statstab::([] file:`$(); algo:`int$(); compressedLength:`long$();uncompressedLength:`long$());\n    / Check if process is single threaded - if multi then compress in parallel then clean up after\n    // Add metrics on any files due to be compressed to be used afterwards for comparison \n    table:update compressionvaluepre:{(-21!x)`compressedLength}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that update table records", "input": "", "output": "statstabupdate:{[file;algo;sizeuncomp;compressionvaluepre]\n        if[not compressionvaluepre ~ (-21!file)`compressedLength;\n            statstab,:$[not 0=algo;(file;algo;(-21!file)`compressedLength;sizeuncomp);(file;algo;compressionvaluepre;sizeuncomp)]]}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that remove records from a table", "input": "", "output": "g:{[f;x]`sym`time xcols delete s from @[;`sym;{$[null y;x;` sv x,y]}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for foo to calculate aggregate statistics", "input": "", "output": "foo:{[d;f;t;g;x]@[;`sym;`p#].Q.dsftg[(dst;\"D\"$-8#string x;d);(` sv src,x;sum t 1;0);f;t;g]}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "endp:{[x;y;z] .tst.endp:@[{1+value x}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement check in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "check:{[fp;dupcheck]\n\tif[dupcheck;\n\t\tif[count select from timer where fp~/:funcparam;\n                        '\"duplicate timer already exists for function \",(-3!fp),\". Use .timer.rep or .timer.one with dupcheck set to false to force the value\"]];\n\t$[0=count fp; '\"funcparam must not be an empty list\";\n\t  10h=type fp; '\"funcparam must not be string.  Use (value;\\\"stringvalue\\\") instead\";\n\t  fp]}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement rep in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "rep:{[start;end;period;funcparam;nextsch;descrip;dupcheck]\n\tif[not nextsch in `short$til 3; '\"nextsch mode can only be one of \",-3!`short$til 3];\n\t`.timer.timer upsert (getID[];cp;start;0Wp^end;period;check[funcparam;dupcheck];0Np;$[start<cp;period*ceiling(cp-start)%period;0D]+start:(cp:.proc.cp[])^start;1b;nextsch;descrip);}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement one in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "one:{[runtime;funcparam;descrip;dupcheck]\n        `.timer.timer upsert (getID[];.proc.cp[];.proc.cp[];0Np;0Nn;check[funcparam;dupcheck];0Np;runtime;1b;0h;descrip);}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement remove in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "remove:{[timerid] delete from `.timer.timer where id=timerid}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named removefunc that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "removefunc:{[fp] delete from `.timer.timer where fp~/:funcparam}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function tablecomp to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "tablecomp:{[tab]\n  (1b;(\"table count of \",(string tab),\" is \",c);c:count get tab)\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement endofperiod in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "endofperiod:{[x;y;z] .tst.eop:@[{1+value x}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named endofday that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "endofday:{[x;y] .tst.eod:@[{1+value x}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function upd to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "upd:{[t;x] .tst.upd:@[{1+value x}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function orderquery to group data by key columns", "input": "", "output": "orderquery:{[queryparams]\n  query:enlist[?],(gettable;getwhere;getby;getselect)@\\:queryparams;\n  renamecolumns[queryparams;query];\n  if[queryparams`optimisation;\n    // If there is no by clause or if the by clause isn't on sym just enlist the query\n    if[0b~@[query;3] ;:enlist query];\n    // If there is a sym in the by clause\n    if[`sym in value query[3];:splitquerybysym[query];]];\n  :enlist query;\n }"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement gettable in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "gettable:{[queryparams]queryparams`tablename}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named getwhere that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "getwhere:{[queryparams]\n  whereclause:extractkeys[queryparams;`instrumentfilter`timefilter`filters`freeformwhere];\n  whereclause:reorderwhere[queryparams;whereclause];\n  :whereclause;\n }"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that group data by key columns", "input": "", "output": "getby:{[queryparams]\n  byclause:extractkeys[queryparams;`timebar`grouping`freeformby];\n  if[()~byclause;:0b];\n  byclause:inter[`date,queryparams`attributecolumn;key byclause]xcols byclause; //- group on `date`sym first (if they exist), then timecol, then remaining args\n  :byclause;\n }"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function getselect to query and filter table data", "input": "", "output": "getselect:{[queryparams] extractkeys[queryparams;`columns`aggregations`freeformcolumn]}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for ffill to calculate aggregate statistics", "input": "", "output": "ffill:{[args]\n\t / - Checks type of each column and fills accordingly\n    forwardfill:{\n        $[0h=type x;\n            x maxs (til count x)*(0<count each x);\n            fills x]\n    }"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for pivot to group data by key columns", "input": "", "output": "pivot:{[args]\n\tcheckargs[args;`table`by`piv`var;(\" sS\")];\n \t/ - Check for optional args f and g\n\t/ - Check if f optional exists, if empty set as default else leave as input\n\tif[not `f in key args;\n\t  args[`f]:{[v;P] `$\"_\" sv' string (v,()) cross P}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "buildquery:{[inputparams]\n  if[.proc.proctype in key inputparams;inputparams:inputparams .proc.proctype];\n  inputparams:.dataaccess.checkinputs inputparams;                                           \n  queryparams:.eqp.extractqueryparams[inputparams;.eqp.queryparams];\n  if[`procs in key inputparams;:(.proc.proctype,.queryorder.orderquery queryparams)]; \n  :.queryorder.orderquery queryparams}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement dataformat in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "dataformat:{[t;d] `name`data!(t;jsformat\\:[d;typemap])}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for updformat to format data for output", "input": "", "output": "updformat:{[t;d] `name`data!(t;(key d)!(d`tablename;jsformat[d`tabledata;typemap]))}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function init to initialize or configure the system", "input": "", "output": "init:{\n new:(x,:()) except t;\n t::t,new;\n w,::new!(count new)#();\n modifier,::new!(count new)#{-8!.j.j updformat[\"upd\";`tablename`tabledata!(x 1;x 2)]}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function del to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "del:{w[x]_:w[x;;0]?y}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named close that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "close:{{.html.del[;y] each .html.t; x@y}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named endp that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "endp:{[x;y;z] .tst.endp:@[{1+value x}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function tablestodatastream that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "tablestodatastream:{[params]\n  defaults:`timer`h`syms`replayinterval`timerinterval`tc`timerfunc`where!(0b;0;`symbol$();`timespan$0n;`timespan$0n;`time;`.z.ts;());\n  params:defaults,params;\n\n  // Check for default parameters `tabs`sts`ets\n  if[count missing:`tabs`sts`ets except key params;'\"missing parameters: \",\" \" sv string missing;];\n  params[`tabs]:(),params[`tabs];\n\n  ds:raze {tabletodatastream x,(enlist `tn)!enlist y}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function getbuckets that retrieve data", "input": "", "output": "getbuckets:{[s;e;p](s+p*til(ceiling 1+e%p)-(ceiling s%p))}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function tabletodatastream to query and filter table data", "input": "", "output": "tabletodatastream:{[params]\n  // Evaluate select statement in HDB\n  t:@[params[`h];\n      (eval;tableselectstatement params);\n      {.lg.e[`dataloader;\"Failed to evauluate query on hdb: \",x]}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function tableselectstatement that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "tableselectstatement:{[params]\n  // Build where clause\n  wherec:(enlist (within;`date;(enlist;`date$params[`sts];`date$params[`ets]))) // date in daterange\n            ,$[count params[`syms];enlist (in;`sym;enlist params[`syms]);()] //if syms is empty, omit sym in syms\n            ,$[count params[`where];params[`where];()] // custom where clause (optional)\n            ,enlist (within;params[`tc];(enlist;params[`sts];params[`ets])); // time within (sts;ets)\n\n  (?;params[`tn];enlist wherec;0b;())\n }"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for gettimers to schedule periodic tasks", "input": "", "output": "gettimers:{[params]\n  times:getbuckets[params[`sts];params[`ets];params[`timerinterval]];\n  ([]time:times;msg:params[`timerfunc],'times)\n  }"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that save data to disk", "input": "", "output": "getTMPSAVE:{`$\":../tmp.\",(string .z.i),\".\",string x}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for append to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "append:{[t;data]\n    t insert data;\n    if[MAXROWS<count value t;\n        / append enumerated buffer to disk\n        .[` sv TMPSAVE,t,`;();,;.Q.en[`:.]`. t]; \n        / clear buffer\n        @[`.;t;0#]; \n        ]}"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named disksort that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "disksort:{[t;c;a] \n    if[not`s~attr(t:hsym t)c;\n        if[count t;\n            ii:iasc iasc flip c!t c,:();\n            if[not$[(0,-1+count ii)~(first;last)@\\:ii;@[{`s#x;1b}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "end:{ / end of day: save, clear, sort on disk, move, hdb reload\n    t:tables`.;t@:where 11h=type each t@\\:`sym;\n    / append enumerated buffer to disk\n    {.[` sv TMPSAVE,x,`;();,;.Q.en[`:.]`. x]}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function exit that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "exit:{ / unexpected exit: clear, wipe TMPSAVE contents (doesn't rm the directory itself)\n    if[not KEEPONEXIT;\n        t:tables`.;t@:where 11h=type each t@\\:`sym;\n        / clear buffer                          \n        @[`.;t;0#];\n        / overwrite written-so-far-today data with empty\n        {.[` sv TMPSAVE,x,`;();:;.Q.en[`:.]`. x]}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement pkg in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "pkg:{.utl.load $[10h ~ type .utl.PKGLOADING;.utl.PKGLOADING,\"/\",x;.utl.PKGLOADING,x]}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement realPath in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "realPath:{\n  rPath:{[absm;p] $[p like absm;p;` sv (hsym `$system \"cd\"), (`$1 _ string p)]}"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that load data from files or databases", "input": "", "output": "loadFile:{[file];\n  f:1 _ string file;\n  if[0i ~ system \"e\";\n    :@[{system \"l \", x;1b}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function getPackageInfo to retrieve data", "input": "", "output": "getPackageInfo:{[loadArg;v;allowReload];\n  $[-11h ~ type loadArg;\n    `file`package!2#$[null[.utl.LOADSTRUCTURE] or loadArg like \"*.q\";loadArg;` sv loadArg,.utl.LOADSTRUCTURE];\n    / If a generic list is passed, we treat it as a symbol and characters, using the symbol as a package name\n    / This is useful to allow requires that reference relative paths\n    0h ~ type loadArg;\n    `file`package!(` sv loadArg[0],`$\"/\" vs 1 _ loadArg;loadArg[0]);\n    .utl.requireVH.findV[loadArg;v;allowReload]\n    ]\n  }"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that group data by key columns", "input": "", "output": "getPackageLoading:{[loadArg;pkgInfo];\n    / Package specified with a file handle using init.q extension\n  $[(-11h ~ type loadArg) and pkgInfo[`file] like \"*init.q\";\n    first ` vs pkgInfo[`file];\n    / Package specified with a file handle and string component using directory path\n    (0h ~ type loadArg) and 11h ~ type key pkgInfo `file;\n    pkgInfo[`file];\n    / All other .q files\n    pkgInfo[`file] like \"*.q\";\n    .utl.PKGLOADING;\n    / The rest (new packages defined by loading argument)\n    pkgInfo[`package]\n    ]\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named initlogger that initialize or configure the system", "input": "", "output": "initlogger:{[inputparams]\n  // Get the request number\n  if[not .dataaccess.logging;:-1]\n  reqno:1+count .dataaccess.stats;\n  `.dataaccess.stats upsert (reqno;.z.u;.z.p;.z.p;.z.w;inputparams;1b;`);\n  :reqno\n  }"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement updatelogger in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "updatelogger:{[reqno;swapdict]\n    if[reqno=-1;:-1];\n    .dataaccess.stats[reqno]::.dataaccess.stats[reqno] upsert swapdict;\n    :-1;\n    }"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function error to update table records", "input": "", "output": "error:{[reqno;error]\n    if[reqno=-1;'error];\n    updatelogger[reqno;`endtime`error`success!(.proc.cp[];`$error;0b)];\n    'error;\n    }"}
