{"instruction": "Write q code for chained to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "chained:{\n  .stplg.ts now:.z.p\n }"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function getdailyadjustment that retrieve data", "input": "", "output": "getdailyadjustment:{exec adjustment from .tz.t asof `timezoneID`gmtDateTime!(.eodtime.datatimezone;.z.p)}"}
{"instruction": "Create a q/kdb+ function adjtime to execute a query and return results", "input": "", "output": "adjtime:{[p]\n     :exec adjustment from .tz.t asof `timezoneID`gmtDateTime!(.eodtime.rolltimezone;.z.p);\n     }"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement getroll in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "getroll:{[p]\n     z:rolltimeoffset-adjtime[p];                           // convert rolltimeoffset from rolltimezone to UTC\n     z:`timespan$(mod) . \"j\"$z, 1D;                         // force time adjust to be between 0D and 1D\n     (\"d\"$p) + $[z <= p;z+1D;z]                             // if past time already today, make it tomorrow\n     }"}
{"instruction": "Write a q function named getday that retrieve data", "input": "", "output": "getday:{[p]\n     p+:adjtime[p];                                         // convert date from UTC to rolltimezone\n     \"d\"$p-rolltimeoffset                                   // adjust day according to rolltimeoffset\n     }"}
{"instruction": "How do I write a q function that retrieve data", "input": "", "output": "gethandle:{exec first w from .servers.getservers[`procname;x;()!();1b;1b]}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for duplicateconfig to update table records", "input": "", "output": "duplicateconfig:{[t] update process:raze[t `process] from ((select from t)where count each t[`process])}"}
{"instruction": "Write q code for readmonitoringconfig to perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "readmonitoringconfig:{[file]\n  // read in config CSV (actually pipe delimited)\n  .lg.o[`readconfig;\"reading monitoring config from \",string file:hsym file];\n  // read in csv file, trap error\n  c:.[0:;((\"SS****NN\";enlist\"|\");file);{.lg.e[`readconfig;\"failed to load monitoring configuration file: \",x]}"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement p in q/kdb+", "input": "", "output": "p:{@[value;x;{[x;y;e] .lg.e[`readconfig;\"failed to parse param value from config file at row \",(string y),\" with definition \",x,\": \",e]}"}
{"instruction": "Implement a function readstoredconfig that perform data operations", "input": "", "output": "readstoredconfig:{[file]\n  // read in the stored config file. Return true or false status\n  // check for existence \n  if[any null file;\n    .lg.o[`readconfig;\"supplied stored config file location is null: not attempting to read stored config\"];\n    :0b\n  ];\n  if[()~key file:hsym file;\n    .lg.o[`readconfig;\"could not find storedconfig file at \",string file];\n    :0b];\n    .lg.o[`readconfig;\"reading stored config file from \",string file];\n    @[{addconfig get x}"}
